  2026-08-05: valid Atom, updated 2026-08-05T20:25:24Z. The timestamps below are
  shifted back one day so they sit before the 03:15 run this suite pins, which is
  the ordinary case anyway: the run happens overnight and the edits happened
  yesterday.

  Atom, not RSS, and the differences are all the ones that break a parser written
  for one of them: the date is <updated>/<published> in RFC 3339 rather than
  <pubDate> in RFC 822, the link is an attribute rather than element text, the
  identity is <id>, and there is a <link rel="self"> that must NOT end up in a
  seed list. Change detection only — a wiki edit is not an event.
-->
